<title>USA: High Plains Wheat - Basis bids weaken further.</title>
<headline>High Plains Wheat - Basis bids weaken further.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Basis bids for hard red winter wheat weakened further at both Gulf and interior locations, grain dealers in the U.S. High Plains said Friday.</p>
<p>Dealers said part of the weakness was coming from the apparent lack of export demand at the Gulf of Mexico.</p>
<p>&quot;I think it's the Gulf. There's no bid down there for deferred months, and we just can't sell what we've got,&quot; a south-central Kansas dealer said.</p>
<p>One exporter's Galveston bid had dropped to 45 cents over the March contract Friday morning, down four cents from Thursday morning's level of 49 cents.  </p>
